-# The queue control for one downloadable asset: "Add to queue", or once added
-# "Remove from queue". It sits in a stable #queue-control-<id> wrapper so the
-# add and remove turbo_streams can swap one for the other. Polymorphic: a
-# content Blob passes `blob_noid:`, an IIIF derivative rendition passes `role:`
-# (its identity has no blob). Both buttons carry `label` so the swapped-in
-# control still names its file.
-#
-# Each aria-label opens with the control's own visible text and appends the
-# file it acts on. WCAG's Label in Name asks that the accessible name contain
-# the visible label, so a name that reads "Add <file> to download queue" fails
-# against a button that reads "Add to queue".
- blob_noid = local_assigns[:blob_noid]
- role = local_assigns[:role]
- label = local_assigns[:label].presence || 'this file'
- queued = blob_noid.present? ? download_queue_includes?(work_noid, blob_noid) : download_queue_includes_derivative?(work_noid, role)
- item_params = (blob_noid.present? ? { work_noid: work_noid, blob_noid: blob_noid } : { work_noid: work_noid, role: role }).merge(label: local_assigns[:label])
%span.ms-2{id: queue_control_id(work_noid, blob_noid: blob_noid, role: role)}
  - if queued
    -# The .turbo_stream path is what asks for the stream: Turbo's Accept header
    -# asks for one on every form, including the queue page's Remove, which must
    -# keep its redirect.
    = button_to download_queue_item_path(item_params.merge(format: :turbo_stream)), method: :delete,
        class: 'btn btn-tonal-danger btn-sm', form: { class: 'd-inline' },
        'aria-label' => "Remove from queue: #{label}" do
      %i.fa-solid.fa-xmark.me-1{'aria-hidden' => true}
      Remove from queue
  - else
    = button_to download_queue_items_path(item_params),
        class: 'btn btn-tonal-secondary btn-sm', form: { class: 'd-inline' },
        'aria-label' => "Add to queue: #{label}" do
      %i.fa-solid.fa-cart-arrow-down.me-1{'aria-hidden' => true}
      Add to queue
